  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a SwiftHFR user editing a message HFR does not let me edit, I want the app to say it was refused, not that the result is unknown, so I neither retry nor wonder whether it went through.\n\n### Facts\n- `W440c` (#440, captured 2026-11-10): a `bdd.php` edit POST of another account's message gets the answer `<div class=\"hop\"> Vous n'avez pas les droits pour éditer ce message ! </div>`. There is no link, no input and no `Refresh`.\n- `HopResponseParser.classify` (LOT-037) calls a `.hop` a refusal only when it has a link or an input. With neither, and no \"avec succès\", it returns `unrecognized`. So `PostingFlow` reports `unconfirmed(.unrecognizedAnswer(message:))` and `MPStorageTransport.save` reports `posting(.unconfirmed(...))`. That is safe, since it is never a success and never retried, but it is wrong: HFR said no.\n- `MPStorageTransportWriteTests.anotherAccountsMessageIsNotASuccess` pins today's behaviour; it changes with this fix.\n\n### Scope\n- Classify this sentence (or the negated, link-less, refresh-less `.hop` shape, if more captures support a rule) as `rejected` under `.write`. Cite `W440c`.\n- Keep `W17c`'s logged-out handling and the success sweep unchanged. Check the corpus sweep for other link-less refusals before generalising (LESSONS: fix the class, not the instance).\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- `W440c` classifies as `rejected` with its sentence, and the MPStorage and Posting flows report `rejected`. The tests fail without the change.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
